#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kdm; provides a graphical interface that allows you to log in to a system. "
"It prompts for login (username) and password, authenticates the user and "
"starts a <quote>session</quote>. &kdm; is superior to &xdm;, the X Display "
"Manager, in a number of ways."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quick Start Guide"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is a quick start guide for users who fit the following pattern:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"X is configured and works with the command <command>startx</command> from "
"the commandline."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each user will generally only use a single window manager or desktop "
"environment, and does not change this choice very often, or is comfortable "
"editing a single text file in order to change their choice."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This scenario will be sufficient for many environments where a single user "
"or several users normally boot the computer and log into their preferred "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting up a Default Session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create or open the file <filename>~/.xinitrc</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you already have a working <filename>~/.xinitrc</filename>, go to the "
"next step"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If one does not already exist, add a line to the <filename>~/.xinitrc</"
"filename> to start your preferred window manager or desktop environment."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "For &kde; you should enter:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "<userinput>startkde</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For other window managers or desktop environments, you should look in their "
"documentation for the correct command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make a link as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>ln</command> <option>-s</option> <parameter>~/.xinitrc "
"~/.xsession</parameter></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At this point, typing <userinput><command>startx</command></userinput> on "
"the commandline should start X, with a &kde; session. The next task is to "
"try &kdm;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, type "
"<userinput><command>kdm</command></userinput> at the prompt."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You should see a login window, which is described more fully in <xref "
"linkend=\"login\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Typing your normal username and password in the fields provided, and leaving "
"<option>default</option> selected as the session type should now open a "
"&kde; session for your user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have other users to configure, you should repeat the procedure above "
"for each of them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a quick guide to getting up and running only. You probably will want "
"to customize &kdm; further, for example, to hide the names of the system "
"accounts, to allow further sessions, and much more. Please read through the "
"rest of this manual to find out how to do these things."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Login Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user interface to &kdm; consists of dialog boxes. The main dialog box "
"contains:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Widgets allowing you to authenticate. When the \"classic\" authentication "
"method is chosen, these are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "A <guilabel>Username:</guilabel> field for you to enter your username."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "A <guilabel>Password:</guilabel> field for you to enter your password."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) a list containing entries with the name and graphical image of "
"each user (for example, a digitized photograph). Clicking a list entry is "
"equivalent to typing the associated username into the <guilabel>Username:</"
"guilabel> field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) a region to the right of or above the authentication area which "
"can be used to display either a static image or an analog clock."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guibutton>Login</guibutton> button that validates the username/password "
"combination and attempts to start a session of the selected type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guibutton>Menu</guibutton> button that opens an action menu with the "
"following items:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) A <guimenuitem>Session Type</guimenuitem> item to choose the "
"type of session (desktop environment, window manager) to start. See <xref "
"linkend=\"different-window-managers-with-kdm\"/> to find out how to "
"configure different session types."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) A <guimenuitem>Authentication Method</guimenuitem> item to "
"switch between different authentication methods like the classical username"
"+password, smartcard, biometry, &etc; The actual authenticators are "
"combinations of <acronym>PAM</acronym> modules and matching frontend modules "
"(<quote>conversation plugins</quote>). See <xref linkend=\"option-"
"pluginslogin\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Switch User...</guimenuitem> "
"item to switch between local sessions running on different virtual terminals "
"of this computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Restart X Server</guimenuitem> "
"item that terminates the currently running &X-Server;, starts a new one and "
"displays the login dialog again. You can use this if the display content "
"seems to be broken somehow."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on remote displays) A <guimenuitem>Close Connection</"
"guimenuitem> item that closes the connection to the &XDMCP; server you are "
"currently connected to. If you got to this server through a host chooser, "
"this will bring you back to the chooser, otherwise it will only reset the &X-"
"Server; and bring up the login dialog again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Remote Login</guimenuitem> "
"item that displays a host chooser dialog with &XDMCP; servers one can log "
"into remotely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally on local displays) A <guimenuitem>Console Mode</guimenuitem> "
"item that terminates graphical login and leaves you at the console. See "
"<xref linkend=\"option-consolettys\"/> and <xref linkend=\"option-servertty"
"\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Optionally) A <guimenuitem>Shutdown...</guimenuitem> item that displays the "
"<guilabel>Shutdown</guilabel> dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Shutdown</guilabel> dialog box presents a set of buttons that "
"allow one of these actions to be executed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turn Off Computer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:285
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shut the system down in a controlled manner, ready for power-down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restart Computer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shut the system down and reboot. For systems that use <application>Lilo</"
"application> or <application>Grub</application>, an optional drop down box "
"allows you to select a particular operating system to be used for the reboot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid "Schedule..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, you may use it to enter a more complex shutdown "
"dialog. See <xref linkend=\"option-scheduledsd\"/> for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing the <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> button returns to the main &kdm; "
"dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kdm;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter assumes that &kdm; is already up and running on your system, "
"and that you simply want to change its behavior in some way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kdm; starts up, it reads its configuration from the folder <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdm/</filename> "
"(this may be <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/kde4/kdm/</filename> or "
"something else on your system)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main configuration file is &kdmrc;; all other files are referenced from "
"there and could be stored under any name anywhere on the system - but "
"usually that would not make much sense for obvious reasons (one particular "
"exception is referencing configuration files of an already installed &xdm; - "
"however when a new &kdm; is installed, it will import settings from those "
"files if it finds an already installed &xdm;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since &kdm; must run before any user is logged in, it is not associated with "
"any particular user. Therefore, it is not possible to have user-specific "
"configuration files; all users share the common &kdmrc;. It follows from "
"this that the configuration of &kdm; can only be altered by those users that "
"have write access to <filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdm/"
"kdmrc</filename> (normally restricted to system administrators logged in as "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can view the &kdmrc; file currently in use on your system, and you can "
"configure &kdm; by editing this file. Alternatively, you can use the "
"graphical configuration tool provided by the &systemsettings; (the "
"<guilabel>Login Screen</guilabel> module in the <guilabel>System "
"Administration</guilabel> category)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The remainder of this chapter describes configuration of &kdm; via the "
"&systemsettings; module, and the <link linkend=\"kdm-files\">next chapter</"
"link> describes the options available in &kdmrc; itself. If you only need to "
"configure for local users, the &systemsettings; module should be sufficient "
"for your needs. If you need to configure remote logins, or have multiple "
"&kdm; sessions running, you will need to read on."
msgstr ""

